WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.060
The bacterium E.

2
00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.980
coli can feed on lactose,
the sugar in milk.

3
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:10.050
With no lactose around, it makes almost
none of the enzymes it needs to use it.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.040
Add lactose, and within
minutes, the enzymes appear.

5
00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:19.120
Making them only when lactose is
present saves energy and amino acids.

6
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.270
So how does a bacterium
know when to start?

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.290
In this mission, you'll
map the lac operon:

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.920
a group of genes transcribed together.

9
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.480
Then you'll read graphs of gene activity,

10
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.420
minute by minute, before
and after a sugar is added.

11
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:39.330
Your mission: find out how a bacterium
knows when to start making its lactose

12
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:40.200
enzymes.
